  "relevance_note": "The paper describes one identifiable patient with a germline TNFAIP3 variant, with individual-level detail in Table 2 ('| Patient 4 | TNFAIP3 (c.1939A>C) | Female, 60 years ...').",
  "method_note": "Read only the paper, the schema and the rules; no script was used, all rows were written by hand. Scope: of the 24 AOSD patients, only the single patient with a TNFAIP3 variant (Table 2 'Patient 4') is in scope; the other four patients with variants (NOD2, TNFRSF1A, SCN9A) have no TNFAIP3 variant and no HA20 diagnosis and got no rows, their number is kept in publications.cohort_size_as_stated = 24. Table 3 (literature review) columns for the prior studies hold cohort-level counts only, no individual-level data, so no rows come from them. Table 3's 'VUS (n)' row for the 'Present study (2024)' column is a stacked cell whose values were on separate lines in one cell ('TNFRSF1A: P75L / NOD2: R675W, E751K / TNFAIP3: T647P / SCN9A: G884S'); each line is labelled with its gene, so I did not assign anything by position, and 'T647P' is recorded as the protein string of this study's single TNFAIP3 variant because the study prints exactly one TNFAIP3 variant (c.1939A>C); the paper never states that T647P is the protein change of c.1939A>C. Table 2 gives ages only as e.g. 'Female, 60 years' without saying whether this is age at diagnosis or at last evaluation; I recorded it under age_at_diagnosis because the study's only age measure is 'Age at diagnosis (years)' (Table 1, range 18-70) and did not fill age_at_last_evaluation. is_proband and cites_prior_report_of_same_patients are false with no span: the paper never calls this patient a proband or index case, is a cohort of 24 rather than a single-patient case report, and never says its patients were published before. The Discussion sentence 'the patient with the TNFAIP variant did not show atypical symptoms' is vague; I kept it as one excluded phenotypic_features row ('atypical symptoms') with a null HPO candidate. The abstract's 'except for one patient with the TNFAIP3 VUS' was not used as a phenotype row because it concerns atypical manifestations and/or treatment refractoriness together. Cohort-level counts in Table 1 were not used to exclude anything for this patient; the only group statement used is 'all patients had elevated acute-phase reactant levels and hyperferritinemia' (checklist item 'elevated inflammatory markers (CRP/ESR)', observed, inferred from group statement). Variant class, zygosity, inheritance, functional evidence and ACMG codes are not reported: the paper classifies the variant only as a VUS and prints no ACMG codes.",
